        "original_id": "a291c5ec-33c4-5899-9545-983962882a87",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Hetfield, Rick Rubin, Bob Rock\n- Organizations: Metallica\n- Products: \"Enter Sandman\", \"Metallica\" (album), Death Magnetic, \"The Unforgiven\", \"Nothing Else Matters\", \"Wherever I May Roam\", \"Sad but True\"\n- Concepts: a child's nightmares\n\nFacts:\n- \"Enter Sandman\" is a song by the American heavy metal band Metallica.\n- Hetfield wrote the lyrics for \"Enter Sandman,\" and the lyrics deal with the concept of a child's nightmares.\n- The 1991 album \"Metallica\" included five singles considered among Metallica's best-known songs: \"Enter Sandman,\" \"The Unforgiven,\" \"Nothing Else Matters,\" \"Wherever I May Roam,\" and \"Sad but True.\"\n- Death Magnetic was Metallica's first album produced by Rick Rubin.\n- Death Magnetic was Metallica's first album since the 1991 album \"Metallica\" not to be produced by Bob Rock.",
